  "telegramApi400Behavior": {
    "useMockTelegramEnv": false,
    "transportKind": "real (https://api.telegram.org)",
    "explanation": "When USE_MOCK_TELEGRAM=false, all outgoing bot replies (ctx.reply / ctx.api.sendMessage) are sent to real api.telegram.org using Bot 2's real token. Because synthetic test tgIds (800001001, 800002001, 800003001..800003010) do not have an active chat with @QuickBook_test_bot on Telegram's servers, api.telegram.org returns '400: Bad Request: chat not found'. Crucially: (1) All PostgreSQL transactions (BotUser upsert, Booking creation with pg_advisory_xact_lock, Booking cancellation) and Redis atomic operations (acquireSlotLock Lua script, releaseSlotLock Lua script, ZADD/ZREM booking:reminders) execute BEFORE the final ctx.reply() and are Durably Committed! (2) Admin notifications in createBooking are wrapped in .catch() so admin 400 errors never abort booking creation. (3) However, because ctx.reply() throws an unhandled GrammyError at the end of the handler, Grammy's session() middleware does not reach its post-next() session save step, and WebhookInboxService catches the error, leaving status='RECEIVED' (attempts=1) or 'FAILED' (after 3 attempts).",
